g momo knows this  is bad and tries to stop the island with  a headbutt but obviously that won't work  as we predicted and as yamato explains  momo has to use his flame clouds to move  the island if his clouds are stronger  than kaidos they can save the capital  and this sounds crazy but it's actually  perfect because kaidos are weakening  with his fight against luffy and soon  they might disappear completely and when  that time comes it's important that  momo's clouds are active obviously momo  has doubts about whether he can do it  but we all know he will at the end of  the day it's perfect for his character  arc to save the capital like this but  still he does call the situation  unbelievable disaster the title of the  chapter it gets worse too as yamato  explains that if luffy beats kaido that  would be even worse because the island  would free fall and the weapons and  gunpowder would explode it would be like  a giant bomb  and nobody in the capital or on the  island would be able to survive so in my  mind this just guarantees that momo will  succeed in using the flame clouds to  save everyone even if it takes a while  to figure it out momo doubting himself  even thinks about stopping luffy so that  kaido doesn't get too drained and yamato  rightfully smacks him on the head for  being a [ __ ] as yamato says so well  luffy willingly put everything on his  shoulders even though he can barely  stand they can't stop him after that  he's the only one that can defeat kaido  and telling him about this would only  burden him more i mean it's already  enough to ask someone to beat the  strongest creature in the world but then  also to beat him with having to worry  about this there's no way that's gonna  happen no they gotta figure it out on  their own while letting luffy do his job  another example of how one piece really  makes teamwork seem important and  emphasizes how it takes more than a  super strong dude to get to your goal  then we go to my other favorite figh